'''Elevate''' (formerly stylized as '''eLevate''') is an [[:Category:United States|American]] esports organization founded in 2012.

==Timeline==
{{tabs dynamic
|This=7
|name1=2014
|name2=2015
|name3=2021
|name4=2022
|name5=2024
|name6=2025
|name7=2026
|content1=
* August 22nd - '''eLevate''' merge with [[Exertus eSports]] and acquire their ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' lineup consisting of [[Warden]], [[Storm]], [[TM]], [[Xp3]], and [[desi]]. <ref name="elevate 2014">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ElevateGG/status/502677886483304448|title=UPDATE: @exertusesports has officially merged with @eLevateGG...|date=2014-08-22|author='''eLevate'''}}</ref>
* September 13th - '''eLevate''' part ways with [[TM]] and sign [[RUSH]] as his replacement. <ref name="elevate rush">{{cite web|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20140927014859/http://elevate.gg/articles/news/general/27/elevate-csgo-team-adds-rush-to-replace-tm|archivedate=2014-09-27|url=http://elevate.gg/articles/news/general/27/elevate-csgo-team-adds-rush-to-replace-tm|title=eLevate CS:GO Team Adds RUSH to Replace TM|date=2014-09-13|publisher='''eLevate'''}}</ref>
* November 11th - '''eLevate''' sign [[Volcano]] as [[desi]] is acquired by [[iBUYPOWER]]. <ref name="desi ibp">{{cite web|url=https://www.gosugamers.net/counterstrike/news/29049-volcano-replaces-desi-in-team-elevate-desi-joins-ibuypower|title=Volcano replaces desi in Team eLevate, desi joins iBUYPOWER|date=2014-11-11|publisher=[[GosuGamers]]}}</ref>

|content2=
* January 8th - '''eLevate''' part ways with [[Volcano]] as they sign [[EliGE]] and [[roca]]. Additionally, they move [[Warden]] to a coaching position. <ref name="eLevate add two">{{cite web|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150111024101/http://elevate.gg/articles/news/general/68/roster-changes-for-elevates-csgo-team-announced|archivedate=2015-01-11|url=http://elevate.gg/articles/news/general/68/roster-changes-for-elevates-csgo-team-announced|title=Roster Changes for eLevate’s CS:GO Team Announced|date=2015-01-08|publisher='''eLevate'''}}</ref>
* January 13th - [[Warden]] is acquired by [[Team Liquid]]. <ref name="CS">{{cite web|url=https://www.teamliquid.com/news/2015/01/13/introducing-counter-strike-global-offensive|title=Introducing Counter-Strike: Global Offensive|date=2015-01-13|author=[[jokasteve]]|publisher=[[Team Liquid]]}}</ref>
* March 22nd - [[EliGE]] is acquired by [[Team Liquid]]. <ref name="+EliGE">{{cite web|url=https://www.teamliquid.com/news/2015/03/23/elige-joins-team-liquids-csgo-team|title=EliGE joins Team Liquid's CS:GO team|date=2015-03-23|publisher='''Team Liquid'''}}</ref>
* March 24th - '''eLevate''' sign [[desi]]. <ref name="desi returns to eLevate">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/14554/elevate-add-desi|title=eLevate add desi|date=2015-03-24 |author=[[stitch]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
* June 1st - '''eLevate''' part ways with [[desi]] and sign [[Professor_Chaos]] as his replacement. <ref name="desi leaves Elevate">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/15085/desi-announces-elevate-exit|title=desi announces eLevate exist|date=2015-06-01|author=[[MIRAA]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
* June 29th - '''eLevate''' part ways with [[roca]] and [[RUSH]]. <ref name="roca and rush released from elevate">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/rocazor/status/615373666092777472|title=Released from @eLevateGG with my boy @eLevateRUSHH, thanks for everything guys|date=2015-06-29 |author=[[roca]]}}</ref>
* July 3rd - '''eLevate''' part ways with [[Storm]] and sign [[daps]], [[aKis]], and [[rooRoooo]]. <ref name="elevate announces new lineup">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/15349-elevate-announces-new-lineup|author=[[stitch]]|title=eLevate announces new lineup|date=2015-07-03|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
* July 7th - '''eLevate''' part ways with [[Professor_Chaos]]. <ref name="professor_chaos steps down">{{cite web |url=https://www.hltv.org/news/15395/professor-chaos-steps-down|author=[[stitch]]|title=Professor_Chaos steps down|date=2015-07-07|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
* July 8th - '''eLevate''' part ways with [[rooRoooo]] and re-sign [[RUSH]]. <ref name="rooRoo leaves eLevate">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/eLevateGG/status/618999210382376960|title=We have officially released @eLevateRooRoo from the #eLevateCSGO roster|date=2015-07-08|author='''eLevate'''}}</ref><ref name="RUSH rejoins eLevate">{{cite web |url=https://twitter.com/elevategg/status/618947254242680832|title=We are happy to welcome back @eLevate_RUSH to the #eLevateCSGO team to replace Professor Chaos|date=2015-07-08|author='''eLevate'''}}</ref>
* July 9th - '''eLevate''' sign [[NAF]] to complete their lineup. <ref name="NAF join eLevate">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/eLevateGG/status/619253460656001026|title=We are proud to announce @eLevateNAF as the fifth player of the #eLevateCSGO roster!|date=2015-07-09|author='''eLevate'''}}</ref>
* August 13th - '''eLevate''' part ways with their roster. <ref name="Elevate released their CS:GO team">{{cite web|url=http://elevate.gg/articles/news/general/130/team-elevate-on-indefinite-hiatus-from-csgo|archivedate=2017-04-26|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170426170552/http://elevate.gg/articles/news/general/130/team-elevate-on-indefinite-hiatus-from-csgo|title=Team eLevate Releases CS:GO Team|date=2015-08-13|publisher='''eLevate'''}}</ref>

|content3=
* April 13th - '''Elevate''' sign [[Patins da Ferrari]], a lineup consisting of [[CutzMeretz]], [[bruno_x]], [[HPS]], [[Demonos]], [[history]], and [[ricdic]], the latter as coach. <ref name="elevate 2021 roster">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ElevateGG/status/1382045931433037824|title=Introducing the Elevate CS:GO roster!|date=2021-04-13|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* May 16th - '''Elevate''' bench [[bruno_x]] and sign [[t9rnay]] as his replacement. <ref name="bruno_x gives way to tunay">{{cite web|url=https://draft5.gg/noticia/bruno_x-da-lugar-a-turnay-na-escalacao-da-elevate|title=bruno_x dá lugar a turnay na escalação da ELEVATE|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|trans_title=bruno_x makes room for turnay in the ELEVATE lineup|date=2021-05-16|author=[[Lucas Benvegnú]]|publisher=[[Draft5]]}}</ref><ref name="t9rnay joins">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ElevateGG/status/1393973258890924033|title=Today we welcome our new CSGO player, @turnayfps welcome to the "bizarros"!|date=2021-05-16|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* June 16th - '''Elevate''' part ways with [[history]] and [[HPS]]. <ref name="history and HPS leave">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/historyfps/status/1405343708875264001|title=Saida da Elevate|trans_title=Departure from Elevate|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|date=2021-06-16|author=[[history]]}}</ref>
* June 17th - '''Elevate''' part ways with the remainder of their roster. <ref name="brazilians leave">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Demonoscs/status/1405566296440385537|title=Salve guys, como vcs ja sabem, o quinteto da elevate ja nao estamos mais juntos|trans_title=Sup guys, as you already know, the Elevate quintet are no longer together|date=2021-06-17|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|author=[[Demonos]]}}</ref>

|content4=
* January 11th - '''Elevate''' sign [[ex-Ceará eSports]], a lineup consisting of [[supLex]], [[skip]], [[naitte]], [[koala]], [[paiva]] and [[luq]], the latter as coach. Additioanlly, they sign [[miolo]] as an analyst and [[danyeL]] as a manager. <ref name="elevate 2022 roster">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ElevateGG/status/1480977818947260417|title=We are BACK!|date=2022-01-11|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* February 9th - '''Elevate''' part ways with [[luq]]. <ref name="luq leaves">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/luqcsgo/status/1491462705928183815|title=Comunicando que não faço mais parte da @ElevateGG e me encontro F/A|trans_title=Announcing that I am no longer part of the @ElevateGG and I find myself F/A|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|date=2022-02-09|author=[[luq]]}}</ref>
* February 13th - '''Elevate''' part ways with [[paiva]]. <ref name="paiva leaves">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/paivacsgo/status/1493019206492860424|title=No último mês pedi desligamento da @ElevateGG|trans_title=Last month I asked to leave @ElevateGG|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|date=2022-02-13|author=[[paiva]]}}</ref>
* February 23rd - '''Elevate''' part ways with the remainder of their roster. <ref name="brazilians leave 2">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ElevateGG/status/1496530954869161987|title=An update on Elevate CSGO|date=2022-02-23|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>

|content5=
* February 15th - '''Elevate''' sign [[timbermen]], a lineup consisting of [[snav]], [[dare]], [[shane]], [[Peeping]], and [[dea]]. <ref name="elevate 2024 roster">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ElevateGG/status/1758246052627349993|title=It's time for the Timbermen to take a new step forward|date=2024-02-15|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* April 13th - '''Elevate''' sign [[m1cks]] as coach. <ref name="m1cks">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/elevategg/status/1779321202177110303|title=Time to add a bigger brain for even bigger plays...|date=2024-04-13|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* June 4th - '''Elevate''' part ways with [[m1cks]]. <ref name="-m1cks">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/elevategg/status/1798142695103213597|title=Ahead of ECL Playoffs, we want to give a heartfelt farewell to coach @joshm1cks|date=2024-06-04|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* July 17th - '''Elevate''' bench [[dea]]. <ref name="bench dea">{{cite web|url=https://www.dust2.us/news/50709/dea-out-at-elevate-in-shock-move|title=dea out at Elevate in shock move|author=[[Mnmzzz]]|publisher=[[Dust2.us]]}}</ref>
* July 24th - '''Elevate''' move [[dea]] back to the active lineup. <ref name="+dea">{{cite web|url=https://www.dust2.us/news/50953/official-dea-returns-to-elevates-starting-lineup|title=Official: dea returns to Elevate's starting lineup|date=2024-07-24|author=[[Mnmzzz]]|publisher=[[Dust2.us]]}}</ref>
* August 31st - '''Elevate''' part ways with their roster. <ref name="-roster">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ElevateGG/status/1829912430463668530|title=Today we part ways with our Counter Strike roster|date=2024-08-31|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>

|content6=
* January 21st - '''Elevate''' sign a new lineup consisting of [[short]], [[zede]], [[Skr]], [[lash]], [[diozera]], and [[zander (Portguese player)|zander]], the latter as coach. <ref name="+chickens">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ElevateGG/status/1881764336437440746|title=We’re back|date=2025-01-21|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* March 17th - '''Elevate''' bench [[Skr]]. <ref name="Skr bench">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ElevateGG/status/1901794283553702173|title=@Skrzik has been moved to the bench and is available for transfer|date=2025-03-17|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* April 17th - '''Elevate''' bench [[short]]. <ref name="short bench">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ElevateGG/status/1912947667753439542|title=@shortfps_ will be moving to the bench. Thank you for your hard work with the team and we hope to see you back soon|date=2025-04-17|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* May 5th - '''Elevate''' sign [[ckzao]] and acquire [[bnc]]  from [[Bounty Hunters Esports]]. <ref name="+bnc+ckzao">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ElevateGG/status/1919543536438976878|title=Filling out the squad|date=2025-05-05|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* August 1st - '''Elevate''' bench [[zede]], [[lash]], and [[diozera]], and part ways with [[bnc]], [[ckzao]], and [[zander (Portuguese player)|zander]]. <ref name="-elevate 2025">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ElevateGG_BR/status/1951385200501588015|title=Nos despedimos hoje da nossa line-up brasileira de Counter Strike 2|trans_title=Today we say goodbye to our Brazilian Counter Strike 2 line-up|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|date=2025-08-01|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* August 3rd - [[short]] is acquired by [[ProCamp]]. <ref name="-short">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/eCampFrankfurt/status/1951937587775484178|title=WE ARE READY for Season 4 of @dachcs Masters|date=2025-08-03|author=[[ProCamp]]}}</ref>
* August 8th - '''Elevate''' loan [[diozera]] to [[Game Hunters]]. <ref name="dio loan">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ElevateGG_BR/status/1953868882843697450|title=Anunciamos a saída por empréstimo do nosso atleta @diozerafps para a Game Hunters CS2|language={{flag|br}} Portuguese|trans_title=We are announcing the loan departure of our player @diozerafps to Game Hunters CS2|date=2025-08-08|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* October 27th - [[diozera]] returns to the bench following the expiration of his loan to [[Game Hunters]]. <ref name="-dio loan">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/GameHuntersCS2/status/1982831081889157214|title=Com o fim do vínculo de empréstimo com o atleta Diozera, a Game Hunters se despede do jogador|language={{flag|br}} Portuguese|trans_title=With the end of the loan agreement with Diozera, Game Hunters bids farewell to the player|date=2025-10-27|author=[[Game Hunters]]}}</ref>
* November 25th - [[diozera]] is acquired by [[ODDIK]] while [[lash]] is loaned to an undisclosed organization,  later revealed to be [[Keyd Stars]]. <ref name="-diozera">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ElevateGG_BR/status/1993418558710129011|title=Hoje nos despedimos oficialmente de @diozerafps e anunciamos que @lashfps foi emprestado para outra organização|trans_title=Today we officially say goodbye to @diozerafps and announce that @lashfps has been loaned to another organization|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|date=2025-11-25|author='''Elevate'''}}</ref>
* December 17th - [[lash]] is acquired by [[Keyd Stars]]. <ref name="lash to keyd">{{inside source|date=2025-12-17|source=lash}}</ref>
|content7=
* April 13th - [[zede]] is acquired by [[Keyd Stars]]. <ref name="-zede">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/VivoKeyd/status/2037243461078766053|title=AGORA É OFICIAL|trans_title=IT'S OFFICIAL NOW|language={{Flag|br}} Portuguese|date=2026-04-13|author=[[Keyd Stars]]}}</ref>
}}

